From 5bbd617e120e310f1f7aa86eb3574f28054e7217 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 22:07:13 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] reaper: a flash releases the USB volumes before it ejects
 them; a boot clears a pending rc_service

Field report (RT-BE86U, Entware on a USB SSD, firmware upgraded from the GUI):
ejusb failed against /tmp/mnt/asus for ~40 s ("Device or resource busy"), fell
back to a lazy detach, and the box flashed with the volume never cleanly
unmounted. The next boot mounted the SSD only after services-start, so dnsmasq
- its log under /opt by the user's dnsmasq.postconf - exited "cannot open log",
and every restart_dnsmasq that followed was refused with "abort the stuck
service ... rc could not be informed (rc_last:restart_upgrade)".

Cause 1: every flash path ejects USB FIRST. httpd's upload handlers, the rc
"upgrade" service and reaper_webs_upgrade.sh all run `ejusb -1 0` before
anything else is stopped, and stock's unmount only stops the NAS services and
the ASUS apps. Entware's daemons (stopped by /jffs/scripts/services-stop,
which only the normal reboot path runs), a dnsmasq logging to /opt and rtrafd
with its history store on the stick all still held files there. Upstream
orders it the same way; Reaper's own flash script copied it.

Fix: rc/reaper_usbrel.c, applet `reaper_usb_release`, run just before each of
those ejects (web.c x5 incl. the factory reset, services.c "upgrade" STOP
branch, reaper_webs_upgrade.sh). It runs services-stop (once per flash),
stops rtrafd, then stops every process that holds anything under /tmp/mnt/ -
cwd, root, exe, an open file or a mapped library - SIGTERM, 5 s, SIGKILL,
logging their names. No-op while no USB volume is mounted; the GUI's own
eject does not call it. watchdog's dnsmasq_check stands down while the
applet's flag exists, so it cannot restart a dnsmasq that would reopen a log
on the volume.

Cause 2: nothing on a boot cleared rc_service. The value that blocked the new
image's first notify_rc could only have been set on the previous image, so
init now unsets rc_service, rc_service_pid and last_rc_service next to the
ASUS_STOP_COMMIT unset - nothing can be mid-service that early.

Not explained by this commit: the reporter's reboot loop. Nothing in Reaper
reboots on a dnsmasq failure; the sys_reboot_reason from that box is owed.

Test: build-scripts/tests/test_usb_flash_release.py compiles the sweep on
the host and runs it against real holder processes, then asserts every flash
eject is preceded by the release; four verify_markers lines.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
